    },
    {
      "id": "j-cp7BQoLTDpsLcrKKZWl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 82.94042911077216,
      "y": 589.3978046841344,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 750,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0L",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 319541436,
      "version": 966,
      "versionNonce": 711307964,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791047886650,
      "created": 1791047495467,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Scale\n- 100M DAU\n- 1M rps\n\n\nNon-functional requirements\n- Availability >> Consistency\n- Low latency rate limit checks (< 10 ms)\n- Scalable to 1M rps\n\nCore Entities\n- Request\n- Client (IP, userId, API key)\n- Rules (100 rps)\n\n\nQuestions\n1. Where should our rate limiter live in our architecture?\n2. How should we identify clients?\n\nAns1:\nIf rate limiter sits in each microservice instance then\nwe can't Guarantee rules.\nIf we put it inside Gateway, there are multiple gateway instance so same\nproblem as above.\nAlso if gateway goes down then our rate limiter is down and backend\nservers are flodded with requests.\n\nSolution: Set a separate Redis cluster for rate limiter.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Scale\n- 100M DAU\n- 1M rps\n\n\nNon-functional requirements\n- Availability >> Consistency\n- Low latency rate limit checks (< 10 ms)\n- Scalable to 1M rps\n\nCore Entities\n- Request\n- Client (IP, userId, API key)\n- Rules (100 rps)\n\n\nQuestions\n1. Where should our rate limiter live in our architecture?\n2. How should we identify clients?\n\nAns1:\nIf rate limiter sits in each microservice instance then\nwe can't Guarantee rules.\nIf we put it inside Gateway, there are multiple gateway instance so same problem as above.\nAlso if gateway goes down then our rate limiter is down and backend servers are flodded with requests.\n\nSolution: Set a separate Redis cluster for rate limiter.\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Wm2l-4-HolqwWLOdk7WEB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 74.23472720121742,
      "y": 1002.7857720659922,
      "width": 11,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0M",
